### Virtual playback sink for the Linux->Windows audio bridge.
### Drop in /etc/pulse/default.pa.d/
###
### Creates a null-sink that Linux apps can play to. The sink's monitor
### source is what windowsspeakers-export.sh streams to Windows over TCP.
### Setting WindowsSpeakers as default-sink means apps go here without any
### per-app configuration -- mirrors WindowsMic being default-source for the
### opposite direction.
###
### Format must match the wire (48kHz s16le stereo) so the monitor doesn't
### resample silently.

load-module module-null-sink sink_name=WindowsSpeakers rate=48000 channels=2 sink_properties=device.description=Virtual_Speakers_To_Windows
set-default-sink WindowsSpeakers
